+# PR #1316 — responsive Analysis evidence renewal
+
+The original mobile research-actions branch is composed with protected `ceb4a7cd9daa8ae8e0483268faa53af30d7876d1`. The source candidate is `a89cb179c0012d0b08b5e8a654de1706f14ba6fe`, tree `b9a6282e627f6b33b07d1912479a95df11175b8b`. The sole textual conflict was the B-F11 source-lock block; product source and its browser specifications composed without textual conflicts.
+
+## Actual qualification
+
+- The incumbent B-F11 producer captured all six desktop/tablet/mobile EN/ZH cases on the composed source. It preserved the language, lex-projection, alternate-listing and origin-context historical appendix.
+- The incumbent B4 producer captured eight desktop/mobile EN/ZH dark/light comparisons. Four dark crops and their authentic log were promoted; light remains an unsupported GAP because each comparison is byte-identical to dark.
+- All six B-F11 screenshots and four dark B4 crops were visually inspected. Controls and copy are visible without overlap or development overlays.
+- Eleven existing evidence-lock tests passed. Full TypeScript passed.
+- Ten existing real-browser cases passed with two intentional non-mobile skips: compact toolbar at 320/390px, bilingual responsive entry behavior, company-scoped thesis navigation, and exact origin-context Save/reopen. Retries were zero.
+- Product and capture-producer source hashes remained unchanged through capture and validation. The browser server on 3567 and B4 server on 3197 were closed afterward.
+
+The raw development logs contain Turbopack HMR subscription warnings. The actual capture waits, screenshots and all focused interaction assertions passed; no production-runtime diagnosis or fix is claimed for those warnings. Log hashes and exact commands are recorded in validation.json; raw stdout stays with this original operation's test-results directory.
+
+## Preserved evidence and limits
+
+The prior current packets are archived byte-for-byte under prior/. Historical recapture records remain intact, including sharedShellCompanyDesignRecapture20261022. This new evidence has its own source identity and timestamps. It does not restamp an earlier capture.
+
+These are local fixture captures and browser interactions. Required natural CI, native integrated queue checks, protected merge and the separately owed authenticated responsive production acceptance remain outstanding.
